========================================================================
(4) n=3: order-2 term reproduces S526 Legendre form; INSIDE DEBT birth
========================================================================
  n=3 pairwise (order-2) overlap vs S526 closed form 1/9+(2/9)chi(a)chi(b)/(ab):
    (a,b)=(1,2): direct|LONELY|=0.000000  S526 closed=0.000000  match=True
    (a,b)=(1,3): direct|LONELY|=0.111110  S526 closed=0.111111  match=True
    (a,b)=(2,3): direct|LONELY|=0.111110  S526 closed=0.111111  match=True
    (a,b)=(1,4): direct|LONELY|=0.166670  S526 closed=0.166667  match=True
    (a,b)=(2,5): direct|LONELY|=0.133330  S526 closed=0.133333  match=True

  INSIDE DEBT = sum of resonance orders r>=3 (the deep diagonals):
    n=3 v=(1, 2): inside-debt(r>=3) = +0.000000   (=0: no 3-term resonance possible with 2 speeds)
    n=3 v=(1, 3): inside-debt(r>=3) = +0.000000   (=0: no 3-term resonance possible with 2 speeds)
    n=3 v=(2, 3): inside-debt(r>=3) = +0.000000   (=0: no 3-term resonance possible with 2 speeds)
    n=3 v=(1, 4): inside-debt(r>=3) = +0.000000   (=0: no 3-term resonance possible with 2 speeds)
    n=4 v=(1, 2, 3): inside-debt(r>=3) = -0.081285
    n=4 v=(1, 2, 4): inside-debt(r>=3) = -0.000000
    n=4 v=(1, 3, 5): inside-debt(r>=3) = -0.000000
    n=5 v=(1, 2, 3, 4): inside-debt(r>=3) = -0.113800
    n=5 v=(1, 2, 3, 5): inside-debt(r>=3) = -0.072575

  => n=3 has NO inside debt (the triangle's only inside is its single
     diagonal-class = the 3-cycle, captured entirely by the order-2 Legendre
     term). The inside debt first switches on at n=4: that is the geometric
     birth of the open case -- the polygon acquires genuine interior diagonals.
